From 48a45d39cf5c5a100a454dcf348f8fd61cdd263e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.net>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 03:19:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] usbhidd: idle rate 0 for keyboards, reports only on change
 (#721)

SET_IDLE with duration 1 asked the keyboard to repeat its report every
4 ms even when nothing changed: 250 transfers a second through xhcid per
keyboard interface, and a pass of usbhidd's report loop for each. The
report handler (rehid) drops values that did not change, so these
reports never produced events; key repeat did not come from them. On a
Pi 400 at idle, usbhidd and xhcid used 9 to 15 % of a core (pi-tests
Test 637).

Duration 0 (indefinite) is what Linux's usbhid and FreeBSD's ukbd set.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/input/usbhidd/src/main.rs | 18 ++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/input/usbhidd/src/main.rs b/drivers/input/usbhidd/src/main.rs
index 86b8f63f..7ac4ffc4 100644
--- a/drivers/input/usbhidd/src/main.rs
+++ b/drivers/input/usbhidd/src/main.rs
@@ -320,15 +320,17 @@ fn main() -> Result<()> {
 
     //TODO: do we need to set protocol to report? It fails for mice.
 
-    //TODO: dynamically create good values, fix xhcid so it does not block on each request
-    // This sets all reports to a duration of 4ms. Only boot keyboards
-    // (interface protocol 1) get it: the idle rate matters for key repeat
-    // reports, and many mice stall SET_IDLE (the HID spec allows that).
-    // FreeBSD's ums does not send it to mice either. A stalled request
-    // used to leave the mouse's next control transfer hanging in xhcid,
-    // which held up every other USB device (#710).
+    // Idle rate 0: the keyboard reports only when something changes, as
+    // Linux's usbhid and FreeBSD's ukbd ask for. A rate of 1 (4 ms) made it
+    // repeat an unchanged report 250 times a second, each one a transfer
+    // through xhcid and a pass of the loop below, for nothing: the report
+    // handler drops values that did not change, so key repeat never came
+    // from those reports. Only boot keyboards (interface protocol 1) get
+    // the request: many mice stall SET_IDLE (the HID spec allows that), and
+    // a stalled request used to leave the mouse's next control transfer
+    // hanging in xhcid, which held up every other USB device (#710).
     if if_desc.protocol == 1 {
-        if let Err(err) = reqs::set_idle(&handle, 1, 0, interface_num as u16) {
+        if let Err(err) = reqs::set_idle(&handle, 0, 0, interface_num as u16) {
             log::warn!("failed to set idle: {}", err);
         }
     }
